{
 "id": "TD-05",
 "system": "ac3",
 "sessionId": "bm-ac2-td-05-8b172fbaaf",
 "endReason": "concluded",
 "customerTurns": 5,
 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "dryer drum wont turn but i can here it running, hotpiont. clothes just sit there"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "From what you have described, the most likely cause is the drive belt. With the dryer unplugged and empty, turn the drum slowly by hand. Does it turn normally, does it feel stiff or stuck, or does it spin round very easily with no resistance at all?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "it spins really easy almost no resistance at all. heard a twang or thud yesterday then just the motor"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Coins, buttons, zips and hair grips are the usual cause. With the dryer unplugged, check the drum and its lifters, the lint filter and the slot it sits in, and turn the drum slowly while you listen. Did you find something (and have you removed it), can you see something stuck that won't come out, or is it all clear?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "nothing caught in the drum no. i looked through the filter slot with a torch and can see a black rubbery strip lying at the bottom"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Does the motor hum/run without the drum turning, does the drum turn freely by hand, or is it stiff to turn by hand?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "motor runs and hums yes, and the drum spins really easy by hand with almost no resistance. warm air is coming out the vent too"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Likely cause: drive belt]\nThe checks point to the drive belt. To find the right part, could you give me the model number? It is usually on a sticker inside the door opening.\n[Panel: \"To check a suitable replacement — Enter your model number below. Once we have the model I can check whether a suitable replacement is available. It's usually on a sticker inside the door or around the frame, or on the back of the appliance.\"]"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "the sticker is half worn off, i can only make out TVHM8 and the rest is gone. is that enough to find the belt or can i look somewhere else for it"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Likely cause: drive belt]\nYes, finding a black rubbery strip at the bottom of the filter slot confirms the drive belt has snapped and fallen into the cabinet. You do not need to search elsewhere for the belt itself as it will be loose inside the drum housing. The checks point to the drive belt. I could not find a confirmed match for model TVHM8 in our parts catalogue, so check with the manufacturer or a parts supplier using the full model number, or ask an appliance engineer to fit it."
  }
 ],
